  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Crowd 1st Set Intro & Tuning**: rare: 6 archived performances [5]\n- **Crowd 2nd Set Intro & Tuning**: rare: 5 archived performances [5]\n- **Passenger**: back after 187 archived shows (2241 days); rare: 9 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-08-08.Cancun_Mike** (recommended): source not stated; 20 songs; 194 min [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-08.aud.cm3.nico11104.flac24**: audience recording; 16 songs; 193 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer attended with wife and daughter, sitting in the 400 level, and chose not to tape so they could watch the screen [3]\n- Reviewer's only in-person Sphere show of the run; they followed the rest of the summer by phone livestream [4]\n- Billed as the Finale of the Dead Forever Sphere run, with Weir, Hart, Mayer and Burbridge listed in the lineup [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-08-08.Cancun_Mike**: taped by Moe Reese; transferred by Eric Lugassy; source: Church Audio CA-14 (omni) Bat2b custom modification > Stereo Breakout > Rode AI Micro > iPhone 14 Pro via Audio Share Application [1]. Also: Lineage: iPhone to WAV, then Reaper, then 24-bit FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2024-08-08.aud.cm3.nico11104.flac24**: taped by Fred Nicolois; transferred by Fred Nicolois; source: Aud>CM-3>F3 [2]. Also: Recorded from the fourth row, in front of John Mayer, in 32-bit float at 48kHz and converted to FLAC [2]",
